  "_doc": "The opening film, shot by shot (story/intro.gd plays this table; docs/ADJUSTING.md 'The opening film'). Shots play in order. Per shot: 'id' (the code that moves the actors is _in_<id> / _run_<id> in story/intro.gd), 'set' (space, vault: the off-world stage; world: the real planet), 'dur' in seconds (a shot grows by itself when a language's subtitle lines need longer), 'fade_in' / 'fade_out' seconds and 'fade_col' [r,g,b] (default black; no fade = a hard cut), 'cam', 'lines' [[second, line key]] (the keys of Intro.lines()), 'sfx' [[second, sound, pitch, dB]], 'cues' [[second, name]] (runs _cue_<name>; a negative second counts back from the shot's end), and 'p' (numbers the shot's code reads). Camera: 'from'/'to' are where it stands at the start and the end, 'look_from'/'look_to' what it looks at, each an [x,y,z] offset from an anchor ('anchor' for the position, 'look_anchor' for the target): '' = the set's origin (the vault's floor centre; in the world, the landing point), 'ark', 'pod', 'lumi', 'glim', 'bin', 'bench'. 'frame': 'pod' turns the offsets with the landed pod (x right of the door, -z out of the door). 'fov' [start, end] in degrees, 'ease' (linear, in, out, inout, inout_cubic, in_cubic, out_cubic, out_quint, smoother), 'roll' [start, end] degrees, 'hand' = hand-held sway in degrees, 'look_lag' = seconds the aim trails a moving subject. 'mode': 'handoff' ends exactly on the game camera; 'orbit' circles 'center' ('angle' [start, end] in degrees from its front, 180 = behind it; 'radius', 'height', 'look_up', 'ahead' as [start, end]); 'over_shoulder' frames 'target' past Lumi. Top level: 'letterbox_px' (bar height), 'door_spot' (where Lumi stops outside the door) and 'end_spot' (where the game starts), both in the pod's frame, and 'end_face' (the yard anchor Lumi faces there).",
